  MF2:  Resolved resonance range  (RRR)                           1925 1451   72
       The RRR was generated with TARES-1.43, compiled on         1925 1451   73
       Nov 12 2021, 12:47:37 at Villigen   , Switzerland. The RRR 1925 1451   74
       expands from 0 to 1.931000E+5 eV. A total of               1925 1451   75
       3 l-values are used and 117 resonances. The resonance      1925 1451   76
       formalism is multi-level Breit Wigner (MLBW).              1925 1451   77
       The TARES database for the measured resonances is          1925 1451   78
        ->  default up to 194011 eV.                              1925 1451   79
       Above this energy, the ladder approach is used.            1925 1451   80
       The ladder approach from the CALENDF code is used to       1925 1451   81
       generate statistical resonances in the unresolved          1925 1451   82
       resonance range. Therefore, the URR is translated into     1925 1451   83
       resolved resonance range. Explanations about the method    1925 1451   84
       can be found in the CALENDF manual: CEA-Report CEA-R-6277  1925 1451   85
       "CALENDF-2010: User manual" by J.C. Sublet, P. Ribon and   1925 1451   86
       M. Coste-Delcaux.                                          1925 1451   87
       The method of creating statistical resonances in the       1925 1451   88
       URR region is described in: "From average parameters to    1925 1451   89
       statistical resolved resonances", D. Rochman et al.,       1925 1451   90
       Annals of Nucl. Ene. 51 (2013) 60.                         1925 1451   91
       The s-wave average level spacing is 14619 eV and           1925 1451   92
       the s-wave neutron strength is 0.00020963 1e-4.            1925 1451   93
                                                                  1925 1451   94
