***************************** T A L Y S **************************1925 1451  189
                                                                  1925 1451  190
TALYS is a computer code system for the prediction and analysis   1925 1451  191
of nuclear reactions. TALYS simulates reactions that involve      1925 1451  192
neutrons, gamma-rays, protons, deuterons, tritons, helions and    1925 1451  193
alpha-particles, in the 1 keV - 200 MeV energy range. This is     1925 1451  194
achieved by implementing a suite of nuclear reaction models into  1925 1451  195
a single code system. This nuclear data file is based on a        1925 1451  196
theoretical analysis that utilizes the optical model, compound    1925 1451  197
nucleus statistical theory, fission, direct reactions and         1925 1451  198
pre-equilibrium processes, in combination with databases and      1925 1451  199
models for nuclear structure. The following output of TALYS is    1925 1451  200
stored in this data file:                                         1925 1451  201
                                                                  1925 1451  202
- Total, elastic and non-elastic cross sections                   1925 1451  203
- Inelastic cross sections to discrete states                     1925 1451  204
- Exclusive channel cross sections, e.g. (n,g), (n,2n), (n,np),.. 1925 1451  205
- Inelastic scattering angular distributions to discrete states   1925 1451  206
- Exclusive channel energy spectra                                1925 1451  207
- Exclusive channel double-differential spectra                   1925 1451  208
- Exclusive gamma production for discrete states and continuum    1925 1451  209
- Elastic scattering angular distributions                        1925 1451  210
- Recoil data                                                     1925 1451  211
- Total particle cross sections, e.g. (n,xn), (n,xp),..           1925 1451  212
- Total particle energy spectra                                   1925 1451  213
- Total particle double-differential spectra                      1925 1451  214
- Isomeric and ground state cross sections                        1925 1451  215
- Residual production cross sections                              1925 1451  216
                                                                  1925 1451  217
For a description of the used nuclear models and their            1925 1451  218
parameterization we refer to [kon19]. If for this specific        1925 1451  219
nuclide we deviate from the global parameterization, it is made   1925 1451  220
explicit above under Nuclide Specific Information.                1925 1451  221
                                                                  1925 1451  222
***************** F I L E   I N F O R M A T I O N ****************1925 1451  223
